test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T23:36:00.5239157Z             "body": "This draft preserves original local stdio MCP and adds bounded batch/jobs, private profiles/artifacts, production packaging and lifecycle controls. Publishing remains disabled; release acceptance is blocked.\n\nCandidateab4e111 fixes the exact Windows initialization failure observed in native98: init RPC timeout at last phase schema_commit, with owned worker close confirmed. Only that case joins the existing bounded initialization retry policy. Each fresh worker revalidates project/key/schema identity; the attempt cap remains three, RPC2000ms/close1000ms/backoff20/40ms remain unchanged. This can consume further initialization attempts after the timeout; it does not extend action/test/job deadlines or replay job mutations. Unconfirmed exits, other phases and incompatible stores remain failures.\n\nIt also publishes checkout-only cancellation witnesses completely before atomic no-replace visibility, retains byte-count and full same-snapshot process diagnostics on failures, and adds matching Chrome fresh-video controls alongside the Chromium control. Original strict assertions and all four possible native98 survivor IDs remain intact. Bounded passive viewport tracing records ACK/resize/first-frame metadata without new protocol requests, timers, renderer warmup or frame discard. Browser core remains reviewed9f9750ae24604e2099e1c1f6564d5d6cb3d19d30dfbc8b5ec61ba18c0989e25a; no additional browser-fidelity fix is claimed.\n\nValidation: actual732c913 Git baseline fails real SQLite pauses before COMMIT and after completed COMMIT before ready/ACK. The candidate recovers both, preserves existing jobs/key, exhausts persistent failure at three attempts, refuses a real intervening future schema without repair, and never retries unconfirmed exit/non-COMMIT timeout. All154 component cases pass on each ordinary-host Node22/24. Actual Chromium/Firefox witness cases and atomic-publication/interruption checks pass on20/22/24; Node20 durable jobs remain unsupported.30 gate calibrations and three passive-trace cases pass. Fresh Node22 production install/all runtime smokes, typecheck, README generation and actionlint pass.194 final source hashes match.297-file pack excludes QA/tests/evidence/workflows;26-doc audit412 local targets/2 anchors has no issues. Initial namespace calibrations fail five ownership checks per LTS because host-root ancestors are unmapped; guards stay unchanged. A local driver bug overwrote those two initial full logs/exit records; visible facts and loss are explicitly recorded. Native CI logs remain retained.\n\nLatest completed native98 at732c913: batch39859258163 reports1626 passes/12 failures; original39859258064 reports599/6; completed summaries2225/18. All18 logs resolve after an empty Windows-client EOF read and successful ordinary retry, with both attempts retained. All five installed-package steps/both parent-death variants and12 actual schema races pass. Windows components145/2 fail during the setup init timeout above; other component lanes146 each pass. Three primary actual Codex1000 clients pass Linux36.088s/Windows38.229s/Mac73.890s, model0/owned0. Separate native Mac timing control passes81.674s:42 progress RPCs max5.846ms,907 reads max19.914ms. This normal sample does not diagnose an earlier failing host or clear native96's Windows CRASHED75 progress timeout.\n\nBatch Linux20/22/24 is209/0,212/1,212/1; Mac210/3 Windows200/5. Two first-JPEG assertions fail despite correct ordering. Mac SDK984/sync980 time out. Linux24 witness JSON ends unexpectedly; original byte length is unlogged. Windows three fresh Firefox variants fail, locator negative fails live factory observation before result validation, and cancellation teardown reports possible IDs5520/6136/6452/6484 without same-snapshot rows/births. No ambiguous-selector success is inferred. Separate pair4 scoped0/legacyOnly2 retains every legacy/root row; helper labels never authorize exclusion. These snapshots stay separate and all four ID-only candidates remain unresolved.\n\nOriginal Linux200/0 Mac199/1 Windows197/3 includes8 stock references each. PNG12/12 PCM11/12 video10/12. Windows WebKit remains ready0 after preload/real activation. Mac Chrome gray is independently confirmed in encoded frame zero: eight actual320x98 input headers despite red320x240 source PNG. The old diagnostic gate excludes this Chrome case, motivating the matching follow-up. Original trusted-code cases pass this sample; Windows legacy1/2 and Docker2/0. Separate healthy controls do not waive main failures or prove transport superiority.\n\nFull scopes/provenance: docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md, docs/evidence/native98-summary.json, docs/evidence/native99-local-verification-proof.json. No role/name/age/window filtering, hint-authorized signals, unsafe replay, lease/debt clearance or retrospective clearance of native94 survivor/native89/96 exits/historical136/142 gaps. Native99 is active atab4e111: batch39868413381 and original39868413347. G18 BLOCKED; no merge/publication.",
